            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            and the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocomplete
          %h3#relative_monads_and_comonads Relative monads and comonads
          %p
            Just as adjunctions give rise to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monads
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonads
          %ol
            %li
              For relative adjunctions, if
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi J
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \dashv_J R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R L
              admits the structure of a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+monad"}
                  monad relative to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            %li
              For relative coadjunctions, if
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %msub
                        %mrow
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi J
                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L {\,\,}_J\!\dashv R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L R
              admits the structure of a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+comonad"}
                  comonad relative to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
          %p (with the units and counits respectively induced as described above).
          %p
            Conversely, there are analogues of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg%E2%80%93Moore+category"} Eilenberg–Moore category
            for relative monads and relative comonads, which induce the relative monads and relative comonads.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %dl
            %dt
              %strong ordinary adjointness
            %dd
              %p
                An
                = succeed "-relative" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi id
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id
                = succeed "-relative" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi id
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id
            %dt
              %strong fully faithful functors
            %dd
              %p
                A functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: A \to B
                is fully faithful iff the canonical natural transformation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \Rightarrow B(F{-}, F{-})
                is invertible iff there exists any such isomorphism, i.e. iff
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mrow
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi F
                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      1 {\,\,}_F\!\dashv F
            %dt
              %strong partially defined adjoints
            %dd
              %p
                As remarked in the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} local definition of adjoint functor
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      L \colon C \to E
              %p
                it may happen that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(L(-),e)
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
                only for
                %em some
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in E
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      J \colon A \to E
              %p
                to be the inclusion of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
                determined by
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(L(-),e)
                representable, and defining
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \colon A \to C
                accordingly, we have
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %msub
                        %mrow
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi J
                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      L {\,\,}_J\!\dashv R
              %p
                This can be specialized to situations such as a category having
                %em some
                but not all
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
                of some kind, partially defined
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} extensions
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"} free object
            %dt
              %strong nerves
            %dd
              %p
                Take
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                a locally small category, and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon A \to B
                a small-admissible functor (one for which
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Fa
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(Fa,b)
                is always small). The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restricted+Yoneda+embedding"} nerve
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                is the functor
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi F
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Set
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      N_F \colon B \to \mathbf{Set}^{A^{\mathop{op}}}
              %p
                given by
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Fa
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_F(b)(a) = B(Fa,b)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                relative to the
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊣
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi y
                              %mi A
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \dashv_{y_A} N_F
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi y
                        %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi F
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta\colon y_A \to N_F F
                is given by the action of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                on morphisms:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi y
                        %mi A
                      %mi a
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi F
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\eta_a \colon y_A a \to (N_F F)(a)
              %p
                at
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a' \colon A
                is
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mi a
                          %mo ′
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi F
                      %mi a
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      F_{a,a'}\colon A(a,a') \to B(F a, F a')
              %p
                Note that, when specialized to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F = 1_A
                %span.newWikiWord
                  full faithfulness
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/full+faithfulness"} ?
                of the
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mn 1
                              %mi A
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi y
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_{1_A} \simeq y_A
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Set
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi y
                        %mi A
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi y
                        %mi A
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      A(x,y) \simeq \mathbf{Set}^{A^{\mathop{op}}}(y_A x, y_A y)
              %p
                In fact, one of the axioms of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+structure"} Yoneda structure
                on a 2-category axiomatises this situation, by requiring the existence of absolute left lifting with respect to Yoneda embeddings, as above: see
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#StreetWalters1978"} Street–Walters
            %dt
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytification"} analytification
            %dd
              %p
                Analytification is a functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi an
                      %mo :
                      %msubsup
                        %mi sch
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mi lft
                      %mo →
                      %mi cas
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^{an}:sch^{lft}_\mathbb{C}\to cas
                from the category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi sch
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mi lft
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sch^{lft}_\mathbb{C}
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"}
                  schemes locally of finite type over
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℂ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
                to the category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi cas
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cas
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+analytic+space"} complex analytic spaces
                = succeed "-relative" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                (resp.,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi cas
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cas
                of (resp.,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi sch
                          %mi ℂ
                          %mi lft
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sch^{lft}_\mathbb{C}
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi lrs
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi ℂ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lrs/\mathbb{C}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi lrs
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lrs
                is the category of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+ringed+topological+space"} locally ringed spaces
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+monad"} relative monad
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            A comprehensive account of relative adjunctions (covering also adjoint functors in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+category+theory"} formal category theory
          %ul
            %li#AM24
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathanael+Arkor"}> Nathanael Arkor
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dylan+McDermott"} Dylan McDermott
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The formal theory of relative monads
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.14014"} arXiv:2302.14014
            %li#Arkor22Thesis
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathanael+Arkor"}> Nathanael Arkor
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Monadic and Higher-Order Structure
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.17863/CAM.86347"} doi:10.17863/CAM.86347
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.repository.cam.ac.uk/bitstreams/666be4fb-957b-4c2e-83fc-8124621f0c43/download"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Arkor-MonadicAndHigherStructure.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p The original reference for relative adjunctions is:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Friedrich+Ulmer"}> Friedrich Ulmer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Properties of dense and relative adjoint functors
              %strong 8
              1 (1968) 77-95 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-8693(68)90036-7"}> doi:10.1016/0021-8693(68)90036-7
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Relative adjunctions were rediscovered in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+monads"} relative monads
            in:
          %ul
            %li#ACU14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thorsten+Altenkirch"}> Thorsten Altenkirch
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Chapman"} James Chapman
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tarmo+Uustalu"} Tarmo Uustalu
              = succeed "," do
                %em Monads need not be endofunctors
              %strong 11
              1:3 (2015) 1–40 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1412.7148"}> arXiv:1412.7148
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.cs.nott.ac.uk/~txa/publ/jrelmon.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2168/LMCS-11(1:3)2015"} doi:10.2168/LMCS-11(1:3)2015
          %p
            For the role of nerves in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+structures"} Yoneda structures
          %ul
            %li#StreetWalters1978
